From e611ba83dceb25b72c3c857856b4dba0b701a430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:43:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 061/294] pvr: lossless TFBC frame buffer compression for
 colour targets

BXM-4-64 (FBCDC algorithm 50, TFBC v1.0) compresses colour attachments in
the PBE and decompresses them in the TPU. Enable it for single-sample,
single-level, single-layer twiddled RGBA8/BGRA8 images used only as colour
attachments and transfer sources (no host, storage or transfer-destination
writers that could bypass the headers). PVR_DEBUG=nofbc turns it off.

Layout, confirmed against the vendor driver: each 8x8 block keeps its slot
in the uncompressed twiddled data and an 8-byte header lives at
data - 8 * (block + 1), growing down. The image gets data_size / 32 bytes
of headers in front and dev_addr points past them. The PBE address now comes
from image->dev_addr rather than the VMA base; without this the headers went
into the neighbouring GPU mapping (corruption, and an MMU fault once the
512 KiB of headers of a 2048x2048 target left mapped VA).

- PBE: compression enabled, 8x8 blocks, direct addressing.
- TPU: FB_DIRECT_8X8 for image views and transfer sources (the RAW32 copy
  path decodes fine).
- The PBE writes whole compressed blocks and zeroes pixels outside its clip.
  For a partial render area, clip to whole blocks and load the attachment in
  the background object whatever its loadOp (a second load-op variant per
  hardware render; dynamic rendering decides at begin). The in-area clear is
  already a draw for partial areas; issue those draws for later hardware
  renders too.
- Transfers into a TFBC image (resolves) compress; a rect that doesn't cover
  whole blocks goes through the clip blit, whose background loads the
  destination.

Known gap: a CLEAR of a TFBC attachment done by a subpass-level (soft)
background object, which only happens when render-level init isn't
possible, with a render area that isn't block aligned, can overwrite up to
7 pixels around the render area.

BXM-4-64 (A733), vkrender 2048 render-only 2.88 -> 2.29 ms, copy 3.96 ->
3.84 ms, render+copy 6.8 -> 6.3 ms/frame. Readback is byte-exact against
PVR_DEBUG=nofbc for 64x64..2048x2048, non-square and noise content,
LOAD_OP_LOAD, unaligned render areas with CLEAR and DONT_CARE, partial
renders, MSAA resolves and two-subpass passes. 9170-case renderpass /
dynamic_rendering / copy_and_blit selection, 5062-case list and buffer copy
list match d253e35 with and without compression; gate 44/44.
